<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharof Rashidov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1983">1983</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sharaf Rashidov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sharof Rashidov was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> writer and politician who led the Communist Party of the Uzbek SSR as first secretary from 1959 until his death in 1983. He built a powerful patronage network and promised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> ever larger <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> harvests. After his death investigations exposed the 'cotton scandal', a vast fraud in which billions of roubles had been paid for cotton that was never produced.</p></div>
